==French==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fr|frm|suyvre}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|sivre}}, {{m|fro|siure}}, {{m|fro|segre}}, from {{inh|fr|VL.|*sequio|*sequere}}, from alteration of {{inh|fr|la|sequī}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|sequor}}. The current French form was influenced by Old French {{m|fro|suit}}, with metathesis from earlier {{m|fro|siut}}, third-person singular present of {{m|fro|sivre}}. Cognate with {{cog|oc|sègre}}, Portuguese/Spanish: ''[[seguir]]'', Italian {{m|it|seguire}}. Compare {{cog|en|sue}}, {cog|en|ensue}} and {{m|en|segue}}.

Cognates among regional languages of France include {{cognate|roa-ang|sieudre}}, {{cognate|roa-brg|seugre}}, {{cognate|pcd|suire}}.

